review_comments.body:
These exception messages are a bit confusing. Especially since it does not appear it is required to omit these fields from the code in `KafkaRaftClient`, and the KIP. How about doing something similar to how `CreateTopicsRequest#build` does validation:

```
public CreateTopicsRequest build(short version) {
            if (data.validateOnly() && version == 0)
                throw new UnsupportedProtocolFieldException("validateOnly", apiKey().name(), version, 1);
```
So for this code something like:

```suggestion
            if (version < 2 && data.voterDirectoryId().equals(Uuid.ZERO_UUID)) {
                throw new UnsupportedProtocolFieldException("A non-zero voterDirectoryId is required in AddRaftVoter version 0 or 1. Upgrade the cluster to support AddRaftVoter version 2 to support a zero voterDirectoryId.");
            }
            if (version < 2 && data.listeners().isEmpty()) {
                throw new UnsupportedProtocolFieldException("A non-empty listeners required in AddRaftVoter version 0 or 1. Upgrade the cluster to support AddRaftVoter version 2 to support a zero voterDirectoryId.");
            }
```

I see that we do this for `AddRaftVoterRequest#build`, but not for `RemoveRaftVoterRequest#build`, can we be consistent? I see that other requests like create topics and fetch have these build time validations, so I am not opposed to add a validation here for v0 and v1.

